  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1033 PM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nThe coming work week remains mostly dry under the influence of a\nlow amplitude ridge with its axis over the central Plains. Some\nof the latest global model guidance shows a very low (10-15%\nchance) of an embedded wave to bring perhaps an outside chance of\na shower for the far NW Panhandles, but chances are not high\nenough to include in forecast at this time. With southerly sfc \nflow continuing and decent H850 WAA into the Panhandles, high \ntemperatures will warm up for next week. Values will return to \nabove average temperatures for the first full week of October.",
